Size: 298972
MD5sum: 55cfa343aefeffb315c555bf64dffe04
SHA1: 2ef3f6821e0a724d0afffa262280f4a7a6953616
SHA256: 27c6f3186014fa4c054b43a96fd09bc1db55b53eb6280067e17d8a6ccd17a522
Section: net
Priority: optional
Description: WCN7880 WiFi bring-up for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Everything the internal WCN7880 (WCN7850-family) WiFi needs on the erhai
 image: modprobe.d policy (blacklist ath12k, no cnss2 auto-load), the
 erhai-wcn-holdfloor / erhai-wcn-devcd / erhai-wcn-wifi systemd units and
 their scripts (erhai-wcn-wifi.sh, save-wcn-devcd.sh, wl_drvcmd), and the
 qcacld config INI (scan_mode_6ghz=0 so 5GHz networks show at cold boot).
 .
 erhai-wcn-wifi.service (oneshot at boot, after NetworkManager) brings the
 station up: wait for the PCIe endpoint, modprobe cnss2 until fs_ready
 appears, trigger the cold-boot calibration, settle, modprobe wlan
 (qcacld-3.0 mission driver from the kernel deb's extra/), detect the
 managed-type netdev, set the country via wl_drvcmd and hand the interface
 to NetworkManager for last-used autoconnect.
 .
 erhai-wifi-discover.service runs erhai-wifi-discover.sh: while the internal
 station is disconnected it fires small-channel-list active scans every 30s
 because the qcacld firmware never probes UNII-1 (ch36-48) in disconnected
 full-band scans — without this, 5GHz APs on UNII-1 are found only by
 passive beacon luck or after connecting on 2.4GHz first.

